## Mode note, stated because the auditor is also the author

`audit_risk_score --plan docs/plan-qor-phase510-reconcile-dialect-accessor.md`
returned `option_b_required: false (no author-momentum risk signal)`.
Independent review was not dispatched for this pass; the justification is
recorded rather than assumed. This is a recomposition of the same two-line
accessor-routing fix (GH #477) already independently reviewed with no defect
found on superseded PR #493 (review `5259248289`, exact head `eda5c4ef`) --
the fix's own diff is unchanged from that reviewed revision; only the base
commit and this phase's governance/version metadata differ.

## Recomposition context

PR #493 sealed this fix against stale base `f3e069b` and independently
claimed the `0.174.1` release slot that PR #492 (Phase 290, GH #482) has
since landed. Per the reconciliation comment on #493
(`5790287629`), #493 is preserved as historical provenance and this phase
recomposes the same code fix plus its regression tests onto current `main`
(`d37c192c`) with fresh governance/CI evidence. No stale version/ledger/seal
metadata from #493 is reused; entry numbers, content/chain hashes, and the
version bump target are computed fresh against the current ledger tail and
`pyproject.toml`.

